Let $t$ be the time in minutes he has to spend walking each day.
The total time spent walking is the number of days multiplied by the time spent walking each day, which is $12 \times t$.
We are given that the total time to break in the shoes is 240 minutes, so we have the equation $12 \times t = 240$.
To find the time he has to spend walking each day, we divide both sides of the equation by 12:
$t = \frac{240}{12} = 20$
So, Jason has to spend 20 minutes walking each day.

